course: dictionary
lesson: 15528
title: Things that follow one another
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Succession is a word for things that come one after another. «The team won three matches in succession.» In succession means the wins came one after another, with no gap between them. Look for clues like after, then, next or one by one.
explain: Succession can also mean the order in which people take over a title or position. «Ella is next in the line of succession to the throne.» Here succession means the order in which people would become king or queen.
explain: A succession of something is a series of it. «A succession of storms hit the coast all week.» That means one storm after another, many times. To check, swap in "a row of": a row of storms still makes sense, so you have understood it.
fact: Succession means a number of people or things that follow one after another.
fact: «In succession» means one after another, without a break.
fact: «In quick succession» means very soon after each other, with little time between.
fact: «Line of succession» means the order in which people take over a title, such as the throne.
fact: In science, ecological succession is the slow change of plant and animal life in an area, such as after a fire.
exercise: «The team won three games in succession.» What does in succession mean here? | In the wrong order | *One after another, without a break | Very fast and very loud | Sadly, at the end
exercise: «After the fire, plants grew back in succession: grass first, then bushes, then trees.» What does succession mean? | A shiny stone | *Things following one after another | A kind of plant | A large fire
exercise: «Ella is next in the line of succession to the throne.» What is the line of succession? | A row of tall trees | A list of the best games | A long line of people waiting for food | *The order in which people take over a title
test: «A succession of loud bangs came from the fireworks.» What does a succession of bangs mean? | *Many bangs, one after another | One very big bang | Quiet bangs at night | Bangs that were sad
test: Mia says, «The rain came in quick succession.» What does quick succession mean? | Without any water | Slowly, with long gaps | Only once at the end | *Very soon after each other
exam: Which phrase means "one after another, without a break"? | *In succession | Line of succession | Ecological succession | Succession of rain
